            type: "Grape",
            name: "Beta",
            category: "American table grapes recommended for Utah",
            harvest_time_unparsed: "Early to mid-season (late summer to early fall)",
            description: "Seedless: No. Trial locations: T. Color: Black. Hardiness zone: 4. Days to maturity: 120+. Small, acidic berries. Also good for jelly. Very prone to iron chlorosis. Similar to Concord in flavor and yields, but ripens 3 weeks earlier. Has not been as vigorous in Utah as reported elsewhere. Source footnote marks this grape as also suitable for juice"
        },
